      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — removing unused imports, constants, fields, and helper methods that aren't needed for this focused test, and adding clear comments to explain the escape-preservation behavior.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports, constants, fields, and helper methods (the original test had many infrastructure methods never called by `testSubstitutePreserveEscape`), replaces the `assertEqualsCharSeq` calls with direct `assertEquals` for clarity, and adds a class-level Javadoc plus inline comments explaining exactly what the escape-preservation behavior means and why each assertion holds."
